<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sandinista National Liberation Front</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1961</span> · Also known as FSLN</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sandinista <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> (FSLN) is a Nicaraguan political party founded in 1961 as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> movement named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-cesar-sandino">Augusto César Sandino</a>. It overthrew the dictatorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anastasio-somoza-debayle">Anastasio Somoza Debayle</a> in 1979 and governed until 1990, fighting the US-backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/contras">Contras</a>, many of them based in Honduras. Its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniel-ortega">Daniel Ortega</a> returned to power in 2007 and has ruled in an increasingly authoritarian way.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sandinista-national-liberation-front.jpg" alt="Sandinista National Liberation Front" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Inti; User:Stannered · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_FSLN.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
